Maya H: Heads up — local onboarding sampleapp with default flags caused a bad retry storm. Started with a few 429s, then retries stacked and event loop lagged. Repro attached.

Maya H: Repro: run sampleapp (defaults) and launch 30 parallel clients that paginate and call embed+chat. Observed repeated 429s and many concurrent inflight sequences.

Owen R: Paste the retry code? Most of these are from immediate retries that don't respect the per-client semaphore.

Maya H: current retry wrapper in sampleapp is naive, basically recursion: `if (retryable) return await fetchPage(cursor)` which re-enters without checking concurrency pool.

Priya K: That recursion can multiply outstanding attempts quickly. Fix is to make retries acquire a slot from the same concurrency pool and do exp-backoff + jitter. Example pattern: acquire slot, try call, release slot, on retry wait then re-acquire.

Maya H: Also saw token refresh churn in some runs where expiry coincided with a burst. JS SDK has single-flight refresh, but sample apps in other languages still show parallel refreshes.

Owen R: Actionable items: (1) implement a retry-queue that acquires the same semaphore before each retry attempt, (2) lower sampleapp default concurrency to 16 and enable a `--burst-safe` mode, (3) add a CLI warning if user sets concurrency > 64 without burst-safe.

Priya K: I'll open a parity PR for Python SDK to add single-flight token refresh and Config.max_sequences (default 16). Also add a small unit test to assert only one refresh occurs under burst.

infra-bot: Created ticket DE-3348: "onboarding: retry-queue + concurrency defaults + SDK refresh parity" assigned to Priya K, Owen R.

Maya H: I'll update sampleapp to use a retry-queue and include a small repro harness in the repo. Will also add a short doc blurb about burst-safety in onboarding.

Owen R: Quick pseudocode for retry-queue to implement in sampleapp:
```
while (attempts < max) {
  await sem.acquire();
  try { return await call(); } catch (e) { if (!retryable) throw e; }
  finally { sem.release(); }
  await sleep(expBackoff(attempts) + jitter());
  attempts++;
}
```

Priya K: We should emit a small telemetry metric (sdk.client.refresh.concurrent_count) so hosted can detect stampedes too.

Maya H: Agreed. Recap: Priya -> SDK parity PR + test; Owen -> sampleapp retry-queue + CLI warning; Maya -> repro + docs. Will attach logs to DE-3348.

Priya K: On it.
